1
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:04,364
Gather round. I've got a scary story.

2
00:00:04,644 --> 00:00:10,656
It's about a kid, his snooze button, and an alarm clock that came back from the dead.

3
00:00:12,036 --> 00:00:14,255
Dylan was always late for school.

4
00:00:14,335 --> 00:00:17,643
Not because he overslept. Because he snoozed. Professionally.

5
00:00:18,023 --> 00:00:23,346
One day he cleaned his room, which is honestly the scariest part of this story.

6
00:00:23,626 --> 00:00:27,224
He tripped over the cord, the alarm clock went dark,

7
00:00:27,604 --> 00:00:30,858
and he plugged it back in like nothing happened.

8
00:00:31,138 --> 00:00:35,281
It blinked back to life. But it wasn't the same clock.

9
00:00:35,861 --> 00:00:40,493
The next morning it went off, and his hand stopped halfway to snooze.

10
00:00:40,773 --> 00:00:44,572
Is that the real time? How long was it dead?

11
00:00:44,752 --> 00:00:46,136
Five minutes? Twenty?

12
00:00:46,616 --> 00:00:49,725
He had no idea. So he got up.

13
00:00:50,305 --> 00:00:52,524
He was on time for days.

14
00:00:52,804 --> 00:00:58,126
Then he worked out the offset, fixed the clock, and was late again by Monday.

15
00:00:59,306 --> 00:01:02,560
Dylan grew up, but he never forgot that clock.

16
00:01:02,640 --> 00:01:07,962
In 2012 he built it as an iPhone app that looked like a slot machine.

17
00:01:08,242 --> 00:01:11,696
He tried to buy LotteryClock.com. The owner said no.

18
00:01:12,276 --> 00:01:15,039
The app never shipped. The idea died.

19
00:01:15,619 --> 00:01:17,838
But some things don't stay dead.

20
00:01:18,218 --> 00:01:20,782
This Kiroween, Dylan dug it back up.

21
00:01:22,462 --> 00:01:23,762
This is LotteryClock.

22
00:01:24,442 --> 00:01:27,006
Pick when you want to wake up.

23
00:01:27,986 --> 00:01:32,274
Then drag the dial to pick how much you're willing to gamble:

24
00:01:32,354 --> 00:01:35,607
five minutes, ten, or forty-five if you're truly unwell.

25
00:01:36,287 --> 00:01:39,541
LotteryClock hides the real alarm somewhere in that window.

26
00:01:39,821 --> 00:01:44,164
Could be early. Could be late. You don't get to know.

27
00:01:44,644 --> 00:01:48,642
Rings early? You win. Snooze guilt-free until your target time.

28
00:01:49,922 --> 00:01:53,776
Rings late? You lose. Get up. You're already late.

29
00:01:54,656 --> 00:01:59,288
And because you can't tell which one it is, you get up anyway.

30
00:01:59,568 --> 00:02:00,868
That's the trick.

31
00:02:01,248 --> 00:02:05,536
Once your clock can't be trusted, your brain can't snooze on autopilot.

32
00:02:06,516 --> 00:02:10,459
Every theme has its own way of telling you you're late.

33
00:02:10,839 --> 00:02:14,638
Good Night. It counts sheep while it decides your fate.

34
00:02:16,318 --> 00:02:19,771
Día de Muertos. Win, and you rest in peace.

35
00:02:22,051 --> 00:02:26,539
Lose, and you rise from the dead. Which is basically every Monday.

36
00:02:27,219 --> 00:02:31,072
Ouija. Let the spirits pick. The spirits say: rise.

37
00:02:31,952 --> 00:02:35,406
Tarot. Push your luck and the card catches fire.

38
00:02:37,686 --> 00:02:40,105
Upright, you sleep. Reversed, you're up.

39
00:02:41,185 --> 00:02:45,673
And for the high rollers: a prize wheel and a poker table.

40
00:02:46,053 --> 00:02:48,617
Two ways to go bust before breakfast.

41
00:02:50,097 --> 00:02:51,397
One more thing.

42
00:02:51,777 --> 00:02:56,264
The website is the game. The iPhone app is the real thing.

43
00:02:56,644 --> 00:02:58,174
Same themes, same dial.

44
00:02:58,454 --> 00:03:03,087
But tap Set Alarm, and it schedules a real alarm with Apple's AlarmKit,

45
00:03:03,167 --> 00:03:05,730
at a random moment inside your window.

46
00:03:06,010 --> 00:03:08,429
The phone knows when. You don't.

47
00:03:09,109 --> 00:03:12,708
When it rings, the alarm tells you how it went.

48
00:03:13,088 --> 00:03:17,576
Rang early? Hit snooze, and you get exactly the minutes you won,

49
00:03:17,656 --> 00:03:20,564
then it rings again at your target time.

50
00:03:21,044 --> 00:03:24,008
Rang late? No snooze. Up you get.

51
00:03:24,688 --> 00:03:29,666
Open the app and the clock rolls to reveal when it really went off.

52
00:03:30,046 --> 00:03:32,264
Every morning lands in your history,

53
00:03:32,344 --> 00:03:36,977
so you can see exactly how many minutes of sleep you've gambled away.

54
00:03:38,257 --> 00:03:39,787
Try it at LotteryClock.app.

55
00:03:40,467 --> 00:03:41,851
Sweet dreams. Maybe.
